    "title": "Between You and Me: Four millennia later, a female finally gets her due - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Leah Dunaief ,\n4 hours ago Since this is the last week of Women’s History Month, I should hurry to tell you about a remarkable woman who lived more than 3400 years ago. Her name was Hatshepsut, and she was “one of ancient Egypt’s few and most successful female pharaohs,” according to a history in this past Tuesday’s edition of The New York Times. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
